From 030e68fe1d753f0f34aedd3ab94f6fa52cd1d69c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pypto-x-agent <pypto-x-agent@local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:23:27 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 112/258] feat(cuda): add cuEvent kernel timing to the PTX
 runtime

Bind cuEventCreate/Record/Synchronize/ElapsedTime/Destroy in the CUDA
driver adapter, expose CudaEvent with idempotent close, and record a
start/stop event pair around the runtime launch path so kernel_seconds,
dispatch_seconds and wall_seconds are reported for every launch.  Event
timing degrades to kernel_seconds=null when the driver lacks the event
API, and events are destroyed in the launch finally block even when a
launch fails.

Add ctypes/mock unit tests, a GamePC cuEvent timing smoke with p50/p95/CV
dispersion and a batch event-vs-wall self-proof, and export the timing
types from pypto.backends.cuda.
